#
# Suderra OS - production-only kernel fragment of the Revolution Pi Connect 4
# (ADR-048 DEC-8.6, ADR-0007 M3, EI-048)
#
# Applied after linux-revpi-suderra.config and the shared arm64 hardening
# fragment, by suderra_aarch64_revpi4_prod_ab_defconfig only: the dev image has
# no module-signing policy of its own (a developer builds and loads modules).
#
# The KUNBUS kernel is a modular distribution kernel and the monolithic
# alternative needs the driver set validated on the board (ADR-0007), so the
# production kernel keeps loadable modules and makes the kernel refuse any that
# its own build did not sign:
#
#   - MODULE_SIG_FORCE: an unsigned module, or one signed by another key, is
#     rejected with EKEYREJECTED whatever the command line says.
#   - MODULE_SIG_ALL: modules_install signs every module, the out-of-tree
#     piControl included (package/revpi-picontrol), with the build's key. The
#     key is generated per build (CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_KEY keeps its default
#     certs/signing_key.pem) and lives only in the build tree; the public half
#     is built into the kernel. A CI build container discards the private half
#     with the rest of the build tree; nothing here persists it.
#   - Lockdown is compiled in at integrity level: the signed-FIT boot chain it
#     was waiting for exists. It stops /dev/mem, kexec of an unsigned image and
#     unsigned module loading independent of lockdown= on the command line.
#     lockdown=confidentiality in the FIT's bootargs still raises it.
#
# Dev and the other ARM boards do not get these lines from the shared arm64
# hardening fragment: tests/image-contracts/arm-hardening-contract-test.sh keeps
# forced lockdown and a disabled MODULES out of it.
#
CONFIG_MODULES=y
CONFIG_MODULE_SIG=y
CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE=y
CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_ALL=y
CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_SHA512=y
CONFIG_LOCK_DOWN_KERNEL_FORCE_INTEGRITY=y
